1. raise "msg": a string is not an exception
   TypeError
2. raise Klass instantiates it with no arguments
   ValueError: args=()
3. raise Klass, "msg" is Python 2 syntax
   SyntaxError
4. raise Klass("msg") is the one form; nothing replaces a message afterwards
   ValueError: args=('an instance',)
5. a bare raise inside except re-raises the same object
   outer got OSError; same object: True
6. a bare raise outside any except: a RuntimeError
   RuntimeError
7. with_traceback replaces the traceback (frames, not strings)
   frames in the borrowed traceback: 2; after re-raising with it: 3
8. no fail alias
   raise is the only spelling
9. raising something that is not an exception
   TypeError
   TypeError
   TypeError
10. sys.exception() inside except, and after it
   sys.exception() is e                    True
   sys.exc_info()[2] is e.__traceback__    True
   sys.exception() after the except        None
11. raise Klass calls Klass(): the constructor, not a hook
   Custom.__init__ called with ()
   Custom
   Custom.__init__ called with ('msg',)
   Custom
